When we have  $19N-21R=355$ , we know that both sides are equal mod  $21$ . Therefore,  $19N\equiv 19N-21R= 355\equiv 19\pmod{21}$ . Divide by  $19$  on both sides,  $N\equiv 1\pmod{21}$  (Note: We can divide like this because  $19,21$  are relatively prime.)

