We have right triangles from symmetry. Let  $AB = DE = 20$  and have vertices in clockwise order. Then  $AD$ ,  $BE$ ,  $CF$  are all diameters and hence all have length  $2r$ . Then let the perpendicular from  $A$  to  $CF$  be  $K$ , and let the center of the circle be  $O$ .Then  $OAK$  is right, and gives,
\begin{align*}
10^2 + AK^2 &= r^2
AK^2 &= r^2 - 10^2
\end{align*}
Similarly  $AKF$  is right so we have,
\begin{align*}
(r-10)^2 + AK^2 &= 22^2
AK^2 &= 22^2 - (r-10)^2
\end{align*}
Then we have,
\begin{align*}
r^2 - 10^2 &= 22^2 - (r^2 - 20r + 10^2)
2r^2 - 20r - 22^2 &= 0
r^2 - 10r - 242 &= 0
\end{align*}
Now solving for  $r$  from quadratic formula we have  $r = 5 + \sqrt{267}$ .

