As  $CEGB$  is cyclic,  $\angle AEG = \angle B = 20^{\circ}$ . This gives  $\angle GEF = \angle AEF - \angle AEG = 50^{\circ} - 20^{\circ} = 30^{\circ}$ . Thus  $\angle MEF = \angle CME - \angle CFE = 20^{\circ} = \angle CFE$  giving  $ME = MF$ . Now  $\angle EMF = 140^{\circ} = 2\cdot 70^{\circ} = 2\cdot \angle EGA$  giving  $M$  is the circumcenter of  $\triangle EGF$ . As  $\angle MFG = 60^{\circ},$   $\triangle MFG$  is equilateral. This gives  $ME = MF = MG = GF$ . This further gives  $\triangle MCE \cong \triangle FEG$  or  $GE = CE$ . 

