&= 2\sum_{i=0}^{1006} \dbinom{2013}{2i}f(x)^{2i}f(1)^{2013-2i},
\end{align*}
which is nonnegative. Since  $(x+1)^{2013}+(-x+1)^{2013}$  can range from  $2$  (when  $x=0$ ) to arbitrarily large, we know that  $f(x)$  is bounded on a nontrivial interval, so  $f(x) \equiv f(1)x$  from Cauchy's functional equation. Since  $f(1^{2013})=f(1)=f(1)^{2013}$ , we know that  $f(1) \in \{-1,0,1\}$ . Thus, the possible answers are  $f(x) \equiv 0$ ,  $f(x) \equiv x$ , and  $f(x) \equiv -x$ .

