One can angle chase to get the result that  $\angle M_BM_AM_C= 90^\circ - \dfrac{\angle BAC}{2}$ (which was a little lengthy for me). The critical observation is to notice that  $\angle M_BM_AM_C$  is half of  $B_1XC_1$  because perpendicular bisector of lines  $B_1A_1$  and  $A_1C_1$  go through the midpoint of the arcs. Finally, 
