In the meantime, we have \begin{align*} 	q &= \frac{be(a+c)-ac(b+e)}{be-ac} 	= \frac{a^2(a+c) - ac\left(b+\frac{a^2}{b}\right)}{a^2 - ac}  	&= \frac{a^2+ac-bc-\frac{a^2c}{b}}{a-c} 	= \frac{ab(a+c) - c(a^2+b^2)}{b(a-c)} \end{align*} Define  $R'$  as the reflection of  $B$  across  $OQ$  in the following way, so that \begin{align*} 	-r'b = \frac{r'-b}{\frac1{r'}-\frac1b} 	&= - \frac{ab(a+c) - c(a^2+b^2)}{b(a-c)} 	\div  \frac{\frac{a+c}{a^2bc} - \frac{a^2+b^2}{c \cdot a^2b^2}} 	{\frac 1b \cdot \left( \frac 1a - \frac 1c \right)}  	&= a \cdot \frac{ab(a+c)-c(a^2+b^2)}{b(a+c)-(a^2+b^2)}  	\implies r' &= -\frac{a}{b} \cdot \frac{ab(a+c)-c(a^2+b^2)}{b(a+c)-(a^2+c^2)} \end{align*} So  $R = R'$ . This completes the proof.

