By the given angle conditions, \(\triangle PAB\sim\triangle PBC\), as well. In addition, observe from \(PD^2=PB^2=PA\cdot PC\) that \(\triangle PAD\sim\triangle PCD\). Therefore, \begin{align*}     \measuredangle QRB&=\measuredangle ARB+\measuredangle QRA=\measuredangle ACB+\measuredangle ACD=\measuredangle ACB+\measuredangle ADP     &=\measuredangle ACB+\measuredangle ADP+\measuredangle BDA+\measuredangle RCA=\measuredangle ACB+\measuredangle BDP+\measuredangle RCA     &=\measuredangle BCA+\measuredangle RCA=\measuredangle ABQ+\measuredangle RBA=\measuredangle RBQ, \end{align*} so \(QB=QR\), as desired.

